title: 'MILESTONE: M2.5 branching FUNCTIONALLY COMPLETE — durable branches merged by meaning, the readiness bar delivered (lock-narrowing the one deferred optimization)'
summary: 'M2.5 — the founder''s readiness bar (work N durable branches at once, merged by meaning, the thing git can''t do) — is functionally complete and correct across 7 commits (af9c2bce, fe7f5219, 40ec9139, a7e9b12e, 1e271752, e0e81f34; +1b2f874a keyed tokens). Delivered: HEAD + merge-base/LCA, DAG-reachable grading, branch/switch/checkout verbs, the weaveTips spine refactor (behavior-preserving), merge-by-meaning with the FAIL-CLOSED rule (Jinx''s divergent-branch falsifier PASSES — config×code and no-shared-token invariant both HELD, not silently sealed), protected main + merge-to-protected human-only (anti agent-self-merge), multi-branch log/diff/show, and the daemon/MCP/descriptor skins. Full suite 1158 passing. The ONE remaining piece is lock-narrowing (per-branch-CAS concurrency win) — deliberately deferred as a correctness-delicate change (C-13: the fabric.jsonl append is not atomic) not needed for correctness or until many-agent scale.'
