body: |-
  WHAT THE FOUNDER CAN DO NOW: warpline init a project; `branch <name>` + `switch` to work a durable feature line; multiple agents/instances fork+propose+admit onto branches; `merge <from>` reconciles BY MEANING — disjoint auto-folds, real conflicts KNOT, and anything meaning is blind to (config×code, scalar-const invariants, .js configs, byte-decided) is HELD for a human instead of silently auto-merged (STRICTLY safer than git); protected main means a swarm can't auto-land into the integration line; `log`/`diff A..B`/`show` navigate the multi-branch history; agents drive it all via the MCP skins with F4-legible descriptors.

  THE DEFERRED PIECE — lock-narrowing (Aegis's concurrency finding): today every write serializes on the single global fabric lock, so disjoint-branch admits that COULD run concurrently (per-ref CAS = per-branch domain) are throttled to serial. Unlocking it requires making the fabric.jsonl append atomic/sharded FIRST (C-13: O_APPEND tears a strand line past PIPE_BUF; the global lock is currently the only thing preventing multi-writer ledger corruption). This is correctness-critical and was DEFERRED rather than rushed at the end of a marathon session — the current global lock is CORRECT (just serial), so M2.5 is complete and safe without it; the win is throughput at N≥3 agents, which is not the current single-machine use. Recommended as a careful standalone next pass. Tracked on T-2026-07-01-017.

  FOLLOW-UPS (all non-blocking, tracked): cross-branch clean switch (expectTreeId baseline — currently needs --force between divergent branches), a dedicated meaning-blind RefusalCode (reuses HELD today), and the criss-cross recursive merge (v1 fails closed).

  ARC: this is the culmination — from the flight-readiness audit through Track-A, the LLM-judge, the pre-fixes, the Tier-1 dogfood, the multi-instance proof, and now M2.5. Warpline now does the multi-branch-by-meaning thing git structurally cannot, on this machine, with the fail-closed safety git can't offer.
